# Closed issues `.foundry/status.md` cites on purpose, and why each is history rather than a gap.
#
# `bin/stale.sh` reports every closed citation. A line here says a person read that one and decided
# it belongs. **An exemption for an issue the page stopped citing is a failure too** — a record of a
# record, and the script says so.
#
# One issue per line: the number, then the reason.

337  named as the owner of a gap it never asked about, and the row now says so
573  cited for a question it settled, and the page now says which half refuses
682  the sign-in question it held, answered for this installation in writing and quoted beside it
711  the harness seam it asked for, disproved rather than built — the page now says so and names no owner
738  one bounded passage, cited as what ran. The row it used to own now says none yet
